    "phase": "paired-progress-before-halo-release",
    "message": "The stable target had no independently painted loading ground while its real external halo remained held",
    "lastProgressAssertion": "No independently painted loading ground before the held halo completed",
    "interpretation": "The fault was acquired, current camera/mask/overlay were stable, another large set of complete source neighborhoods was available over the network, yet the old engine kept only canonical z12 ground. Exact old source has no per-cell commit path: full vector and relief batches await allSettled and their shared Promise.all before replacing ground. The held halo is sufficient to keep at least one required relief unresolved and therefore prevent that shared commit. This is an expected application progress regression witness, not a fixture acquisition failure.",
    "limitations": [
      "No worker completion/profile events or per-cell bitmap readiness were collected. Network completion does not prove decode completion or worker availability. Do not claim 29 decoded pairs.",
      "The held URL was not the only unfinished source: two other DEMs were still in flight and eight required outer-ring URLs had not been observed. Do not claim it was the sole contributor to total load time.",
      "The failure PNG is after release; pre-release evidence is the exact frame and live Network/Fetch snapshots. No successful pending/final pixel comparison exists on the baseline.",
      "This bounded fault witness is not a provider-speed benchmark, smoothness pass, Android pass, or claim about new candidate runtime."
    ]
  },
